Negative control for the add-session reroute (parity cell P10 · AC7.2 · AC1.2 ·
H5).

Puts `addSession` back to what it did before T5.3: a navigation AWAY to the
`useAuth` page for the picked scope, carrying the same `fresh` marker. The pool
is untouched — the same controls, in the same order, with the same labels ("Log
in as staff" with no staff session, "Add another staff session" with one), the
same addable-scope derivation and the same four `actor-scope-add-*` hooks. Only
the destination changes: the page the pool was opened over is left, instead of
the auth overlay opening over it at the actor the control named.

The mutant deliberately keeps the `fresh` marker, keeps the picked scope, and
keeps pushing SOMETHING, so a spec that only asserts "a navigation happened",
"the target carries `fresh`" or "the target names staff" stays GREEN under it —
which is the point: none of those was ever testing the reroute. Only an
assertion that names the overlay target (`<page>--auth`, the page's own params,
the page underneath still the one the pool was opened on) can tell the two
apart.

Re-cut for `R6-15b`: the control's own scope is now carried to the overlay
(`{ actor: scope, fresh: true }`), so both the docblock and the pushed target
moved. The mutation is still the same one — the destination.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: session-switcher.spec.ts — the P10 case(s) asserting that adding a session
opens the auth overlay over the current page rather than routing to `useAuth`.

